From: maxuellstalin <maxuellstalin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:01:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(stream): fail fast on a silent 429 (log poll from
 upstream PR #35)

Carries only the log-poll half of neerazz/hermes-antigravity-oauth#35
(commit ae081e2): the stream's idle path tails the isolated agy log once a
second and raises the RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED error as soon as agy logs its first
retry, instead of waiting out agy's ~140 s of silent internal retries.

Left out on purpose: the `--print-timeout 240s` argv default and the
print_timeout result mapping. agy 1.5.15 documents the flag only as a "time
limit for print mode"; whether it bounds one turn or the whole resident
stream-json worker is not documented, and a session-wide limit would kill the
worker after 240 s. The mapping's message is also Portuguese UI text.
